/* HOST PATCH — applied to the DI-03 package drop, re-apply on DI-04.
   Two projection constants are changed; nothing else in this file is touched.

   1. .stage perspective: 1500px -> 2600px  (line with "perspective:" in MINDMAP_TEMPLATE)
   2. layout(): this.gap=.245*w -> this.gap=.285*w

   Why: every layer draws its leader label at the same SVG coordinates (x=126,
   baselines y=102 and y=120), so the only thing that separates one label from
   the next on screen is its plane's Z offset, projected. Layer 05 is the one
   three-line label — it adds a baseline at y=84 — and it lands in the slot the
   projection has already squeezed hardest. Two things squeeze it: perspective
   1500px over a +/-345px stack scales the near planes up and the far planes
   down, so the screen gap between adjacent labels fell away down the stack
   (63 / 34 / 28 / 25 / 23 / 20px at a 470px layer); and rotateZ(-24deg) shears
   each label, so a wide line spans more screen height than its leading alone.
   At the 4th slot the sum went negative: "Flex-rigid PCB / rigid island" and
   "Thermal foam / isolation / pocket" overlapped by 4.6px at a 470px layer,
   and by 2.9-4.1px everywhere else the 3D stack was used.

   2600px moves the camera back so the six slots are close to even rather than
   3:1 top to bottom; .285 then buys every slot the room the three-line label
   needs. Neither number states anything about the assembly: explode distance
   is already variable at runtime (the slider drives it from 0 to this gap),
   and perspective is the camera. The layer geometry, the rotations, the layer
   width, the 2.25x stage and all seven SVGs are untouched, so the host's own
   copy of that arithmetic in Patch.jsx still holds.

   Note for the next drop: the package's HOST-INTEGRATION.md still documents
   1500px and 0.245x. */
